// load_use.hex
//
// HAZARD UNDER TEST
//   Load-use interlock. A load is followed immediately by an instruction that
//   reads the loaded register. Forwarding alone cannot fix this: the data does
//   not exist until the load's MEM stage completes, which is the same cycle the
//   consumer would need it in EX. The pipeline must stall one cycle.
//
//       cycle        1    2    3    4    5    6    7
//       i0 lw        IF   ID   EX  MEM   WB
//       i1 consumer       IF   ID   ID   EX  MEM   WB
//       bubble                      EX  MEM
//
//   In cycle 3 the hazard unit sees id_ex_mem_read with id_ex_rt = r7 matching
//   if_id_rs = r7, so it drops pc_write and if_id_write and injects a NOP into
//   ID/EX. i1 sits in ID for cycle 4. By cycle 5 the load is in MEM/WB and
//   ForwardRs = 10 supplies the loaded word.
//
//   Why the stall is load-bearing: without it, i1 would be in EX in cycle 4
//   while the load sat in EX/MEM, so the forwarding unit would match on
//   ex_mem_rd and drive ForwardRs = 01 -- handing over ex_mem_alu_result, which
//   for a load is the *address*, not the data. r8 would come out 0x00000000
//   rather than 0x00000014. The test therefore distinguishes a missing
//   interlock from a working one, not merely a missing forward.
//
// CYCLE COUNT
//   13 cycles for the last instruction to retire, and exactly 1 stall cycle.
//     8 instructions
//   + 4 cycles of pipeline fill (the first retires in cycle 5, not cycle 1)
//   + 1 interlock stall
//   = 13
//   The run asserts stalls == 1 by counting cycles in which pc_write is low.
//   That count is what makes the claim checkable rather than a comment. It also
//   holds after the hazard unit gains its read mask: this is a genuine
//   load-use, rs really is read, so a correct unit stalls here too.
//
// EVIDENCE
//   r8. Nothing after index 1 writes it.
//
// POSITIVE CONTROL
//   r7 = 0x00000014 proves the load itself executed and that data memory came
//   out of reset holding 20 in word 0, which is where the expected value comes
//   from. Without this a zero in r8 would be ambiguous.
//
// INDEPENDENT WITNESS
//   dmem word 8, a different word from the one the load read, so the witness
//   cannot be confused with the source data. Reset leaves it 0x00000000, so
//   0x00000014 there is unambiguous proof the store ran with the right value.
//
// EXPECTED FINAL STATE
//   r7          = 0x00000014
//   r8          = 0x00000014   <-- 0x00000000 if the interlock never fires
//   dmem[8:11]  = 0x00000014
//   dmem[0:3]   = 0x00000014   unchanged, the load does not write
//   stalls      = 1
//
// 0: lw  r7, 0(r0)          loads 0x14 from dmem word 0
8C070000
// 1: ori r8, r7, 0x0000     consumer, forces the one-cycle interlock
34E80000
// 2: nop
00000000
// 3: nop
00000000
// 4: nop
00000000
// 5: sw  r8, 8(r0)          witness into a different word
AC080008
// 6: nop
00000000
// 7: nop
00000000
